---
import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { APP, OPERATOR } from '../../config';
import { ROUTES } from '../../i18n';
---

<PageLayout
  locale="en"
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How Ride Streak handles your data: no accounts, no ads, no selling. Your rides stay on your iPhone."
  paths={ROUTES.privacy}
  lastUpdated="6 September 2026"
  intro="This policy covers the ridestreak.de website and the Ride Streak iPhone app."
>
  <h2>1. Controller</h2>
  <p>
    The controller under the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR) is:<br />
    {OPERATOR.name}<br />
    {OPERATOR.street}<br />
    {OPERATOR.postalCode} {OPERATOR.city}<br />
    Germany<br />
    Email: <a href={`mailto:${APP.supportEmail}`}>{APP.supportEmail}</a>
  </p>

  <h2>2. The website</h2>

  <h3>2.1 Hosting and server logs</h3>
  <p>
    This site is served by GitHub Pages (GitHub, Inc., 88 Colin P Kelly Jr
    Street, San Francisco, CA 94107, USA). When you open a page, GitHub
    processes technically necessary connection data — in particular your IP
    address, the date and time of the request, the page requested and your
    browser and operating system. The legal basis is Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR; the
    legitimate interest is the secure and stable operation of the site.
    Transfers to the USA rely on GitHub's standard contractual clauses. See the
    <a
      href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement"
      rel="noopener"
      target="_blank">GitHub Privacy Statement</a
    >.
  </p>

  <h3>2.2 No cookies, no tracking</h3>
  <p>
    This site sets <strong>no cookies</strong>, embeds no advertising networks
    and performs no cross-site tracking. That is also why there is no consent
    banner.
  </p>

  <h3>2.3 Fonts and external content</h3>
  <p>
    All fonts are served <strong>from this server</strong>. There is no
    connection to Google Fonts or any other font CDN, so no IP addresses are
    passed to third parties. Images, scripts and stylesheets are self-hosted
    too.
  </p>

  <h3>2.4 Contacting us</h3>
  <p>
    If you email us, we process what you send purely to answer your enquiry
    (Art. 6(1)(b) or (f) GDPR). Messages are deleted once the matter is closed
    and no statutory retention period applies.
  </p>

  <h2>3. The app</h2>

  <h3>3.1 Principle</h3>
  <p>
    Your cycling data lives on your iPhone and in Apple Health. Nothing is
    uploaded unless you explicitly turn it on. Using Ride Streak requires
    <strong>no account</strong>. There are no ads, no profiling and no sale of
    data.
  </p>

  <h3>3.2 Apple Health (HealthKit)</h3>
  <p>
    With your permission, Ride Streak reads workout and health data from Apple
    Health — cycling workouts, distance, duration, elevation, heart rate,
    energy burned and body weight. This data is processed on your device only
    and is <strong>never</strong> transmitted to us or to third parties. You
    can withdraw access at any time under Settings → Privacy &amp; Security →
    Health. Apple Health data is never used for advertising and never shared.
  </p>

  <h3>3.3 Strava (optional)</h3>
  <p>
    If you choose to connect Strava, Ride Streak fetches activities and profile
    values through the official Strava API — including power, cadence,
    segments, laps, heart-rate zones, FTP and weight. Authorisation happens via
    OAuth directly with Strava; we never receive your Strava password. The
    retrieved data is stored locally on your device. The legal basis is your
    consent under Art. 6(1)(a) GDPR. Disconnecting removes all imported Strava
    data from the app. Strava's own
    <a href="https://www.strava.com/legal/privacy" rel="noopener" target="_blank"
      >privacy policy</a
    > applies in addition.
  </p>

  <h3>3.4 RideStreak Cloud (optional, opt-in)</h3>
  <p>
    RideStreak Cloud is off by default. When you switch it on, only
    <strong>daily training summaries</strong> are transmitted and stored on servers
    in the European Union:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Date</li>
    <li>Duration</li>
    <li>Distance</li>
    <li>Elevation gain</li>
    <li>Training load (as a daily figure)</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    <strong>Not transmitted:</strong> GPS routes, raw heart-rate data, photos,
    per-ride power data, or anything about your bikes and components. Training
    load is calculated on your device; only the finished daily number is
    synced. The legal basis is your consent (Art. 6(1)(a) GDPR). You can
    withdraw that consent at any time in the app's settings and delete your
    account together with all server-side data there.
  </p>

  <h3>3.5 iCloud sync</h3>
  <p>
    With Ride Streak Pro, the app syncs your bikes, parts, rules, tours and
    goals through your private iCloud database. That data sits in your Apple
    account, not with us, and we cannot access it. Apple's privacy policy
    applies.
  </p>

  <h3>3.6 Purchases</h3>
  <p>
    Ride Streak Pro is sold through the Apple App Store. Payment data is
    handled exclusively by Apple; we receive no card or billing details, only
    an anonymous purchase status used to unlock features.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Your rights</h2>
  <p>Under the GDPR you have the right to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>access the data held about you (Art. 15)</li>
    <li>have inaccurate data corrected (Art. 16)</li>
    <li>erasure (Art. 17)</li>
    <li>restriction of processing (Art. 18)</li>
    <li>data portability (Art. 20)</li>
    <li>object to processing (Art. 21)</li>
    <li>withdraw consent with future effect (Art. 7(3))</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Write to <a href={`mailto:${APP.supportEmail}`}>{APP.supportEmail}</a>. You
    also have the right to lodge a complaint with a data protection supervisory
    authority (Art. 77 GDPR).
  </p>

  <h2>5. Changes</h2>
  <p>
    We update this policy when the app or the site changes. The version
    published here is the one that applies.
  </p>
</PageLayout>
